WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.893
Meet the supplied Mesh2Motion fox, with forty-nine bones and fourteen animation clips.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.487
We're inspecting its walk, not creating a new rig.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.339
One moment, four useful views: surface, mesh, skeleton, and side profile.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:15.380
They show the same walk, each revealing something different.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.547
Now slow the walk and follow how the legs bend.

00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:21.652
Watch the same pose across all four views before judging it.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.461
Pause here, and compare the pose in each panel.

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.844
Then let the walk resume, keeping your eye on the changing silhouette.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.912
The mesh shows the surface structure; the skeleton shows the moving joints.

00:00:36.052 --> 00:00:38.633
Use both to spot bends that deserve a closer look.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.784
Before a longer video, check the full cycle for awkward bends and clipping.

00:00:43.924 --> 00:00:47.508
Four views help inspection; they don't guarantee perfect animation.
